# tend root for informalize run `{{run_id}}` — phase `{{phase}}` of `{{informalize_id}}`

Generated by `cf plan-informalize`. Do not hand-edit: regenerate instead, so `run.yaml` keeps
recording the prompt and gate files that were actually used.

| | |
|---|---|
| entrypoint | `{{entrypoint}}` (the output repository at `{{base_commit}}`, plus `tasks/`) |
| gate (out of tree) | `{{gate_dir}}/{{gate_script}} --gate-config {{gate_dir}}/gate.json` |
| task manifests | `{{gate_dir}}/tasks/<task-id>.json` |
| the library's source | `{{library_src}}` (read-only) |
| bridge | `{{bridge}}` |
| model | `{{model}}` |
| tasks | {{task_count}} |
| concurrency | {{max_workers}} workers / {{max_reviewers}} reviewers |

`gate/` holds the informalize gate, the findings gate it imports, `tex/` (the LaTeX runtime the
gate builds with, and the worker's build and check tools), `declarations.json`, `hypotheses.json`,
`data/` (what this phase reads of the previous one), the task manifests and `gate.json`, which pins
the sha256 of every one of them. `bin/` holds the bridge and every helper it calls. Each task
changes only the paths its manifest lists, and its task file's status line.

Start with a **1/1 smoke test** and watch one task through worker, gate, reviewer and merge before
raising the limits; the spend cap is `run.yaml`'s `budget.max_cost`, which the watchdog drains at.
